      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3826945243,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Should a zero-length \"compressed\" block just expand to a zero-length \"decompressed\" block? Do we handle zero-length uncompressed blocks in BLF files?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-09-13T17:34:44.665Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-09-14T08:12:16.469Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 530994271,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 26465,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3828637997,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "1\\. Zero-length compressed blocks:\n\n\\- If decompressed length is 0 (real_length == 0), blf_pull_logcontainer_into_memory() already skips it cleanly at line 1038 without attempting decompression.\n\n\\- If compressed length is 0 (data_length == 0) while real_length \\> 0, the file is corrupt. Even an empty valid zlib stream is at least 6 bytes (header + checksum), so decompressing non-zero bytes from 0 bytes is impossible. Returning WTAP_ERR_BAD_FILE is correct.\n\n2\\. Zero-length uncompressed blocks:\n\n\\- Uncompressed containers (BLF_COMPRESSION_NONE) with real_length == 0 are also skipped at line 1038.\n\n\\- Standalone objects require object_length \\>= header_length (\\>= 16 bytes) in blf_find_next_logcontainer(), so 0-length object headers are rejected with WTAP_ERR_BAD_FILE.\n\n\\- Inside containers, blf_read_block() always advances by at least 16 bytes via MAX(MAX(16, header.object_length), header.header_length).",
          "author": {
            "id": 42208592,
            "username": "meel-ayush",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "meel-ayush",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/929c5e111094e6604a975a84c6b8e8aaee8eaafeac0bbb98330a668fd79efb45?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/meel-ayush"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-09-14T08:12:16.408Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-09-14T08:12:16.408Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 530994271,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 26465,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3829524434,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> If compressed length is 0 (data_length == 0) while real_length \\> 0, the file is corrupt. Even an empty valid zlib stream is at least 6 bytes (header + checksum)\n\nDoes this mean that the compressed length must be at least *6* bytes to be valid, not just > 0?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-09-14T11:00:02.593Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-09-14T11:00:02.593Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 530994271,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 26465,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3829702076,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Technically yes—a valid zlib stream is at least 6-7 bytes (2-byte zlib header, minimal deflate block, and 4-byte Adler-32 checksum), so anything smaller is definitely malformed.\n\nHowever, \\`compressed_len == 0\\` was the specific case causing the division-by-zero crash (\\`decompressed_len / compressed_len\\`) and the assertion failure. For \\`1 \\<= compressed_len \\< 6\\`, division-by-zero does not occur, and \\`inflate()\\` safely rejects the truncated stream with \\`Z_DATA_ERROR\\`, which is already handled cleanly.\n\nI kept it as \\`compressed_len == 0\\` to let zlib handle format validation, but if you prefer an explicit early check for \\`compressed_len \\< 6\\`, I am happy to update it!",
          "author": {
            "id": 42208592,
            "username": "meel-ayush",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "meel-ayush",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/929c5e111094e6604a975a84c6b8e8aaee8eaafeac0bbb98330a668fd79efb45?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/meel-ayush"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-09-14T11:24:59.288Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-09-14T11:24:59.288Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 530994271,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 26465,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3831553356,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> For `1 <= compressed_len < 6`, division-by-zero does not occur, and `inflate()` safely rejects the truncated stream with `Z_DATA_ERROR`, which is already handled cleanly.\n\nThen checking for `compressed_len == 0` is sufficient.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
