      "title": "blf: reject zero-length compressed containers to prevent divide-by-zero",
      "message": "blf: reject zero-length compressed containers to prevent divide-by-zero\n\nWhen parsing compressed Vector BLF capture files, data_length was passed to g_try_malloc() assuming it returns NULL when data_length is 0. In GLib, g_try_malloc(0) returns a non-NULL pointer, allowing a compressed container with data_length == 0 to pass into blf_decompress_zlib() with compressed_len == 0.\n\nIn blf_decompress_zlib(), ws_assert(compressed_len != 0) aborted the process in debug builds, while in release builds (with assertions disabled), computing decompressed_len / compressed_len caused a fatal floating point exception (division by zero, CWE-369).\n\nExplicitly reject data_length == 0 in blf_pull_logcontainer_into_memory() with WTAP_ERR_BAD_FILE, and replace the reachable assertion in blf_decompress_zlib() with an error return.\n",
      "author_name": "Ayush Meel",
      "author_email": "ayushmeel.dev@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2026-09-11T17:57:42.000+05:30",
      "committer_name": "Ayush Meel",
      "committer_email": "ayushmeel.dev@gmail.com",
